`tempSvg` is appended to `document.body` to allow layout measurement, but `tempSvg.remove()` (line 72) is only called on the success path. If `configureLabelImages` or `getBoundingClientRect()` throws, the hidden SVG element leaks into the DOM permanently. Wrap the measurement block in a `try/finally` to guarantee cleanup:
```js
try {
  await configureLabelImages(div.node(), node.label);
  // ...bbox logic...
} finally {
  tempSvg.remove();
}
```
